ocus on the intersection of STEM (mathematics, information technology, natural sciences, and technology) and the visual arts, a concept it refers to as MINKT. \n\nThe school believes that integrating the arts into STEM fields motivates students to engage deeply with scientific activities. This interdisciplinary approach allows STEM concepts to be presented in innovative, visual ways, helping students express their ideas through models, graphics, and descriptive communication.\n\nCurriculum and Academic Program\n\nMentora Gymnasium offers a national curriculum aligned with the requirements for the Abitur and the Mittlere Reife. Students follow a structured academic program with a distinct mathematical and natural science orientation. The institution is classified as a state-recognized substitute school (staatlich anerkannte Ersatzschule) and includes provisions for second-chance education (Zweiter Bildungsweg).\n\nSpecial academic features include:\n\nProject-based learning, where individually determined focus areas are integrated into compulsory elective subjects and conducted during weekly project days.\n\nLanguage and International Orientation\n\nThe school places particular importance on an international orientation and language learning. The foreign language curriculum is structured to support this global perspective, with English offered as the first foreign language and Spanish introduced as the second foreign language. \n\nFacilities and Resources\n\nLocated at Salzufer 6, the school campus is equipped with facilities designed to support everyday school life. These include a cafeteria and a kiosk for student meals and refreshments. The building is accessible, featuring barrier-free toilets and ramp access. To further support families, the school offers full-day care (Ganztagsbetreuung) services.", "geo_country": "DE", "school_type": "Gymnasium", "schulnummer": "04P35", "crime_source": "Kriminalitätsatlas Berlin per Bezirk", "open_days_en": null, "tuition_tier": null, "traegerschaft": "Privat", "tuition_notes": "No fee information found in search results. Website content pages (Main, Fees/Tuition, Admissions, About, Curriculum) were not provided in search results.", "besonderheiten": null, "description_de": "Das Mentora Gymnasium in Charlottenburg wurde im Jahr 2020 als staatlich anerkannte Ersatzschule gegründet und richtet sich an Schülerinnen und Schüler der Klassenstufen 7 bis 12. Ein zentrales Merkmal des pädagogischen Konzepts ist der sogenannte MINKT-Ansatz, der Mathematik, Informatik, Naturwissenschaften und Technik eng mit der bildenden Kunst verknüpft. Dieser interdisziplinäre Weg soll wissenschaftliche Inhalte durch kreative und visuelle Methoden greifbarer machen. Der Lehrplan orientiert sich an den Anforderungen für das Abitur sowie die Mittlere Reife und setzt einen deutlichen Schwerpunkt auf mathematisch-naturwissenschaftliche Kompetenzen. Ein besonderes Highlight im Schulalltag sind die wöchentlichen Projekttage, an denen die Jugendlichen in projektbasierten Lernformen individuelle Schwerpunkte vertiefen können. Die internationale Ausrichtung wird durch das Fremdsprachenangebot mit Englisch und Spanisch gestärkt. Auf dem barrierefreien Campus am Salzufer wird zudem eine Ganztagsbetreuung inklusive schuleigener Cafeteria angeboten. Es ist jedoch zu beachten, dass die Schule in offiziellen Verzeichnissen aktuell als Einrichtung ohne aktiven Schulbetrieb geführt wird.", "description_en": "Mentora Gymnasium, founded in 2020 in the Charlottenburg-Wilmersdorf district, is a private secondary school designed to guide students from grade 7 through to their Abitur. The school's educational philosophy is built around the 'MINKT' concept, which uniquely integrates STEM subjects with the visual arts to foster deep engagement with scientific activities. This interdisciplinary approach encourages students to express complex ideas through innovative models and graphics. The curriculum follows national standards with a strong orientation towards mathematics and natural sciences, complemented by a focus on project-based learning. Every week, dedicated project days allow students to explore individual interests within their elective subjects. To prepare students for a globalized world, the school offers an international perspective with English as the first and Spanish as the second foreign language. The campus at Salzufer 6 features barrier-free facilities, a cafeteria, and full-day care services to support families. Please note that official registries currently list the institution as having no active school operations.", "gruendungsjahr": null, "lehrer_2022_23": null, "lehrer_2023_24": null, "lehrer_2024_25": null, "lehrer_current": null, "belastungsstufe": null, "crime_data_year": "2025", "crime_rate_year": 2025, "metadata_source": null, "tuition_display": "Contact school", "crime_area_level": "district", "crime_change_pct": -14.7, "data_school_year": null, "env_aqi_category": null, "geo_municipality": "Berlin", "lehrer_data_year": null, "plz_interpolated": true, "plz_sensor_count": 0, "poi_kita_01_name": "Kita an der Technischen Universität Berlin", "poi_kita_02_name": "宿舍楼下的幼儿园", "poi_kita_03_name": "Villa Luna", "schueler_2022_23": null, "schueler_2023_24": null, "schueler_2024_25": null, "schueler_current": null, "transit_bus_name": "Marchbrücke", "crime_assault_avg": 1336, "crime_robbery_avg": 137.2, "crime_safety_rank": 10, "crime_vs_city_pct": 38.0, "migration_2023_24": null, "migration_2024_25": 38.9, "migration_current": 38.9, "plz_avg_v85_speed": 25.1, "transit_bus_lines": "245", "transit_rail_name": "U Ernst-Reuter-Platz", "transit_tram_name": "U Turmstr.", "admission_notes_de": "Das Mentora Gymnasium ist laut Schulportrait der Senatsverwaltung für Bildung, Jugend und Familie (Berlin.de) derzeit nicht im Schulbetrieb. Daher sind keine aktuellen Aufnahme-/Anmeldekriterien oder Anmeldezeiträume verfügbar.", "admission_notes_en": "According to the school portrait of the 